# --- Nothing new at the repository root without saying so ----------------------
#
# A mutation harness wrote its scratch into a worktree root and a `git add -A` swept
# **176 files** into a commit -- names like `, kind: operator, line: 1033}` -- so more
# than half of what this repo tracked was debris. The warning below about agent
# worktrees already existed; it did not generalise to "anything else at the root".
#
# So the root is an allowlist: ignore everything there, keep every directory, and name
# the four files that belong. A genuinely new top-level file needs a line here, which
# is the point -- it makes adding one a decision rather than an accident.
#
# **This block must come first.** `!*/` re-includes every directory, so anything that
# ignores a directory has to be stated *after* it or the negation wins. Putting this
# at the end silently un-ignored `build-asan/` and the pre-commit hook caught it.
/*
!*/
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/CMakeLists.txt
!/README.md

# --- Build output, which the rule above would otherwise have re-admitted --------
build/
build-*/
compile_commands.json
.cache/
*.csv

# Three mutation harnesses live in this tree and each is a Python module as well as
# a program. Running one is harmless; *importing* one -- which is how you check its
# substitution patterns still apply without spending an hour finding out -- drops a
# `__pycache__` next to it. That is the same class of debris as the 176 files above.
__pycache__/

# Agent worktrees and transient session state only -- .claude/settings.json is
# project configuration and is tracked deliberately.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/state/
